@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] local-pbr-patch-is-opt-in
The patched crates MUST retain upstream licenses and source provenance, and mark each local change with a `Hakuba:`
comment. A change MUST be opt-in by view, camera or resource, unless it is listed in vendor/README.md as changing
what every view draws (today the last cascade's fade and the moving crossfade dither) or as keeping the same results
(the concurrent preprocessing passes). Forward-motion comparison views MUST keep the original prepass and TAA inputs
until their motion output and temporal edge quality have been validated. Shader output fields, render targets, view
bindings and dynamic offsets MUST use one mode key. The Metal backend MUST present frames as upstream until the game
sets a shortest time on screen.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:architecture] dependency-patch-has-one-copy
Each patched crate (Bevy's PBR renderer, wgpu's HAL) MUST be selected through the project-local Cargo patch. Runtime
and exporter builds MUST NOT read or modify a shared registry source or require a dependency checkout outside this
game. Upstream feature-gated library and shader files MAY remain together, with their purpose documented in the
vendor README. The game MUST reach a patched crate's additions through its Rust API, never through exported C
symbols.
